Subject: [PATCH 45/47] media: mediatek: seninf-camsv: sensors on CSI ports
 0-2, D-PHY

Give the seninf subdev one sink pad per CSI port. The sensor whose link
is enabled streams; only one sink link can be enabled at a time, which
is how the libcamera simple pipeline sets the links up. The route from
the CSI port to CAMSV2 tag 2 is unchanged.

CSI port N uses PHY A/B at +0x8000 * N, SENINF_(2N+1) and its own efuse
word. Add the 4D1C D-PHY setup of the isp7sp seninf driver: four data
lanes with the clock on PHY A lane 2, a 100 ns settle at the 312 MHz
seninf clock, HS prepare, deskew, and the equaliser setting for lane
rates up to 2.5 Gbps, chosen from the sensor link frequency.
